  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>AB</mi></math> is an elementary reaction.</p><p>For a certain quantity of reactants, if the volume of the reaction vessel is reduced by a factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math> the rate of the reaction increases by a factor of _____ . (Round off to the Nearest Integer).</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "27",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Reaction : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>AB</mi></math></p><p>As the reaction is elementary, the rate of reaction is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mo>]</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math></p><p>on reducing the volume by a factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math> the concentrations of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> will become 3 times and hence, the rate becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></math>&nbsp;times of initial rate.</p>"
  }
}